DERIVED DATA SUBSET — AIRCRAFT TYRES

src/data/tyres.js is a DERIVED SUBSET of the Goodyear Aircraft Tire Data
Book (2018, effective 6/18), generated by tools/extract-tyres.py. The data
book is published freely by The Goodyear Tire & Rubber Company and states
that its civil aircraft tire data are in accordance with Tire and Rim
Association standards and conform to FAA TSO C-62e; Goodyear and T&RA are
the owners of that material and it is NOT reproduced here.

What is carried is the thirteen engineering quantities that a 14 CFR 25.733
tyre selection and the strut sizing downstream of it read — rated load,
rated inflation, maximum braking and bottoming loads, outside diameter,
section width, static loaded radius and flat-tyre radius — keyed by the
Goodyear part number so that any row can be traced back to the printed
page. The book's wheel and rim manufacturing columns are deliberately not
carried. This is a derived work for engineering computation, not a reprint
of the book, and anyone needing the full data — including the columns
omitted here, and any revision later than 2018 — should obtain it from
Goodyear directly.
